WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:19.000
[Music]

2
00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:20.500
Hey, y'all, I'm Campbell.

3
00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:21.360
I'm Ivy.

4
00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:22.040
I'm Madison.

5
00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:23.200
And we're all sophomores.

6
00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:24.200
It's actually funny.

7
00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:27.760
We all met in the spring before coming
to Ole Miss at a grad party in Dallas.

8
00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:29.818
After the grad party,
we all stayed in touch,

9
00:00:29.818 --> 00:00:32.700
and I just knew they were gonna
be our best friends in college.

10
00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:34.964
Going into rush week, we were
pretty conflicted and just getting

11
00:00:34.964 --> 00:00:36.980
pulled in so many different
directions from other people.

12
00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:40.053
Every time I left Chi O
and every time I walked past

13
00:00:40.053 --> 00:00:42.700
it on the way to Martin,
I just wanted to go back.

14
00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:43.900
I loved it so much.

15
00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:45.887
I would, like, see the rush chairs
at the top of the steps just,

16
00:00:45.887 --> 00:00:47.440
like, smiling, and I was like,
I want to be there.

17
00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:51.999
I remember going into Madison's room
during rush week and just asking

18
00:00:51.999 --> 00:00:56.360
her if she felt the same level
of comfort and peace at Chi O as I did,

19
00:00:56.360 --> 00:00:58.220
and when she did, I was so happy,
and I knew that's where we wanted to be.

20
00:00:58.420 --> 00:01:00.340
I remember feeling all
the pressure from everyone,

21
00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:03.360
and I just, like, walked into
Chi O and just felt home.

22
00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:06.220
It's truly a testament of what Chi O is.

23
00:01:06.340 --> 00:01:07.700
You'll never stop making friends.

24
00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:16.300
[Music]

25
00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:17.600
Hi, I'm Kennedy Bryant.

26
00:01:17.780 --> 00:01:18.800
I'm from Frisco, Texas.

27
00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:21.300
And I'm Alexa Beatty,
and I'm from Lawrence, Kansas.

28
00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:23.672
Being out of state,
both of us didn't really know a lot

29
00:01:23.672 --> 00:01:25.520
of people coming to Ole Miss
from our high schools.

30
00:01:25.520 --> 00:01:29.480
I moved around my whole life, so I didn't
know anyone except for the Rebelettes.

31
00:01:29.600 --> 00:01:34.021
We were actually set up by some of our
mutual friends to be roommates in Crosby,

32
00:01:34.021 --> 00:01:38.000
and I just remember when we first met,
we instantly became best friends.

33
00:01:38.100 --> 00:01:41.843
It was just such a blessing to come into
somewhere new, and it being so scary

34
00:01:41.843 --> 00:01:44.079
with college and everything,
just to feel like

35
00:01:44.079 --> 00:01:46.120
you already have your person was so lucky.

36
00:01:46.380 --> 00:01:48.808
Going into rush week,
me and Kennedy actually

37
00:01:48.808 --> 00:01:50.913
decided not to tell each other anything

38
00:01:50.913 --> 00:01:53.449
we were doing,
just because we wanted to choose

39
00:01:53.449 --> 00:01:55.500
for ourselves where we found our home.

40
00:01:56.060 --> 00:02:00.800
And for me, every time I walked into Chi O,
I felt that genuineness across the room.

41
00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:03.900
And I just knew that that's
where I needed to be.

42
00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:07.171
The opening of our bids and finding
each other in the Grove and getting

43
00:02:07.171 --> 00:02:10.020
to run home with each other was
just one of my favorite memories.

44
00:02:10.180 --> 00:02:12.622
It felt really special,
both choosing for ourselves but

45
00:02:12.622 --> 00:02:15.020
knowing this is both where
we're meant to be together.

46
00:02:15.300 --> 00:02:21.000
[Music]

47
00:02:21.100 --> 00:02:24.560
On bid day, we actually went
to the Chi O retreat together.

48
00:02:24.820 --> 00:02:26.200
We didn't know a soul on that bus.

49
00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:30.640
We had no clue what was going on,
and now those are some of our best friends.

50
00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:34.380
I don't think I could have gone through
college without Kennedy by my side.

51
00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:37.140
I really, it's really
just the little moments

52
00:02:37.140 --> 00:02:39.300
that really make
our friendship so special.

53
00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:44.900
[Music]

54
00:02:45.020 --> 00:02:50.220
So now we've gone from Crosby to the Arbors,
and now we're in the Brown House,

55
00:02:50.300 --> 00:02:52.963
which is a passed-down
house in Chi O, and there's

56
00:02:52.963 --> 00:02:55.680
been years and years
of Chi Os who have lived here.

57
00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:58.355
I really can't thank Chi O
enough for all the friendships

58
00:02:58.355 --> 00:03:00.620
and all the memories that
will truly last a lifetime.

59
00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:15.300
[Music]
